# Settings for one gdrive-sync profile. install.sh copies this file to
#   ~/.config/gdrive-sync/<profile>/config.env
# and writes the remote and the local root into it. Uncomment the rest of the
# lines you want to change.
#
# The file is optional. Without it the defaults shown below are used.
#
# One Google account is one profile. Profiles are equals: there is no default
# account, nothing is shared between them, and each one has its own copy of
# this file, of folders.txt and of filter.txt.
#
# NOTE: the file is executed as bash code (source). Write only variable
# assignments into it, and keep its permissions to yourself (chmod 600).

# rclone remote name (rclone config). A trailing colon is optional. Each
# account needs a remote of its own — see the README, "Prerequisites".
#GDRIVE_REMOTE=GoogleDrive

# Local root directory the folders are synced under. The default carries the
# profile name, because two profiles sharing or nesting their local roots is
# the one configuration that loses data: each one's bisync would see the
# other's files as local changes and carry their absence to its own Drive.
# gdrive-sync refuses to run when it finds such a pair.
#GDRIVE_LOCAL=$HOME/GoogleDrive/<profile>

# Profile and config directory. These two are an exception: both are read
# before this file is read, so setting them here has no effect. Use the command
# line or the environment:
#   gdrive-sync --profile=work --status
#   GDRIVE_CONF_DIR=~/somewhere-else gdrive-sync --status
#GDRIVE_PROFILE=work
#GDRIVE_CONF_DIR=$HOME/.config/gdrive-sync/<profile>

# The roots the profile directories live under. Same exception: read before
# this file, so set them in the environment if you move them.
#GDRIVE_CONF_ROOT=$HOME/.config/gdrive-sync
#GDRIVE_STATE_ROOT=$HOME/.local/state/gdrive-sync

# State directory: pinned folder IDs, the lock file and status.json. Per
# profile, which is what lets two profiles sync at the same time without a
# shared lock.
#GDRIVE_STATE_DIR=$HOME/.local/state/gdrive-sync/<profile>

# Folder list and rclone's filter file. In the profile's config directory by
# default.
#GDRIVE_FOLDERS=$HOME/.config/gdrive-sync/<profile>/folders.txt
#GDRIVE_FILTER=$HOME/.config/gdrive-sync/<profile>/filter.txt

# --- gdrive-watch -----------------------------------------------------------
# The watcher listens for local changes and syncs the changed folder right away.
# The timer stays as it is, for changes on Drive's side. One watcher instance
# per profile: gdrive-watch@<profile>.service.

# Debounce in seconds: how long changes must be quiet before the sync runs.
#GDRIVE_DEBOUNCE_SEC=5

# Retry in seconds, when the previous run was still going (the lock was held).
#GDRIVE_RETRY_SEC=30

# Which gdrive-sync to run: a name on PATH or a full path. The systemd unit sets
# this itself, because a user session's PATH does not necessarily include
# ~/.local/bin.
#GDRIVE_SYNC_BIN=gdrive-sync
